Grabbed
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/signal_array]

# --- COLOR ---
# [] the patient weight of Veran's hand on your shoulder
# [] Chorik's knuckles white as he starts to turn
# [] the brass button at Chorik's throat catching the late sun
# [] the dun canvas of Veran's uniform stretched across his back
# [] the sound of Veran's leather belt creaking as he stands still
# [] the metallic taste of the air when the wind shifts
# [] the way Chorik's boot scrapes on the rock as he shifts his weight
# [] the fourth man's breath held steady as he watches you
# [] the weight of the interval bell hanging quiet on Veran's belt
# [] the smell of hot metal carried on a sudden gust
# [] the pylon's struts humming with stored energy
# [] the shadow of the pylon stretching long across the mesa
# [] the heat rising in shimmering waves from the bedrock
# [] the smell of oiled leather from Veran's belt
# [] the crew's shadows merging as they close ranks
# --- end ---

FIXME(action): Veran's hand is on your shoulder. He is not gripping hard. He is being patient with you. The crew is not coordinated yet. Behind him Chorik is starting to turn. The housing is still right there.

choices:

* Break free and finish it = Get loose, get to the housing
    @if check combat correct:rush wrong:outlast {
        FIXME(action): You drop your shoulder under his hand and twist. He goes off balance. You are on the housing before he has recovered. The latch plate breaks under your second hit. You strip the activator unit out and break it across your knee. The signal cuts. The pylon goes dark.
        +open "Aftermath"
    } @else {
        FIXME(action): You try to twist. Veran takes you down. Baret is on your other side before you can recover. The two of them put you on the ground. Something hits you wrong on the way down and the world goes white at the edges and then black.
        FIXME(dread): You come to in pale morning light. You are off the mesa road, in the lee of a slab of rock. Your pack is next to you. There is a half-full waterskin beside it. The work site above you is empty. The tower stands complete and humming on the rock. The crew is gone. The wound at your side is shallow but it is not closing on its own.
        +skip_time morning
        +add_condition injured
        +finish_dungeon
    }

* Back off slow = Hands where they can see them, no sudden moves
    FIXME(action): You raise your hands, slow. You take a step back from Veran. He releases your shoulder without comment. He does not move to follow. The other three watch you, calm and attentive in the way of people who are about to firm up and have not quite yet.
    FIXME(horror): You back away from the housing, eyes on them, hands still visible. Each step you take from the tower, the signal in your skull thins by a degree. By the time you are forty paces out the schematics have receded to a low hum. You know now not to get close to one of these again.
    FIXME(dread): You watch from the rocks at a safe distance as the crew completes their transition and finishes packing the tools. They form up and start east down the mesa road toward the next build site, wherever that is. The pylon hums behind them. There is nothing you can do about it.
    +finish_dungeon
    +add_level
